tchup against the Packers. Atlanta has struggled offensively with Cooper Rush and Jack Strand as the team's quarterbacks over the last two weeks, scoring just 16 total points while Rush and Strand accounted for seven turnovers. However, Penix led the Falcons' offense to 20.6 points per game while throwing for 220.2 yards per game when healthy in 2025, suggesting improvement could be coming. Penix will be in for a tough matchup though, as Green Bay's defense has given up just 19.2 fantasy points per game to opposing QBs this season.","4":"Michael Penix is expected to lead Atlanta's offense into the Week 4 matchup against the Saints. The 2024 first-round pick was impressive in his 2026 debut, throwing for 256 yards, one touchdown and one interception in a win against the Packers. Despite playing in the same division as New Orleans, Penix has never played a game against the Saints before. Following his Week 3 performance, the expectation is for Penix to elevate Atlanta's offense by getting the ball into the hands of Bijan Robinson and Drake London. Penix is in for a relatively favorable matchup as well, with the Saints' defense allowing 20.8 fantasy points per game to opposing quarterbacks this season.","5":"Michael Penix will look to stay hot in the Falcons' Week 5 matchup against the Ravens. Penix has been great through two starts in 2026, throwing for 479 yards, two touchdowns and an interception. He's helped rejuvenate Atlanta's offense, as the team has scored a whopping 40 points per game since his return. Despite this, Penix is in for a tougher Week 5 matchup against a Ravens defense that's allowed just 18.8 fantasy points per game to quarterbacks this season.","6":"Michael Penix (ribs) will lead the Falcons' passing attack if active during the Week 6 matchup against the Bears. Penix was productive for the third consecutive game before exiting with a rib injury in the overtime loss to the Ravens, throwing for 240 yards and a touchdown. Through three weeks, Penix is averaging 239.7 passing yards and a touchdown per game. He's in for a favorable matchup if ready for Week 6, as the Bears' defense just allowed Jordan Love to throw for 367 yards and two touchdowns.","7":"Michael Penix will continue leading the Falcons' offense during the Week 7 matchup against the 49ers. Penix was productive despite a loss in Week 6, throwing for 225 yards and three touchdowns while also completing two two-point conversions. Since returning from injury, Penix has led the Falcons' offense to 31.5 points per game, the second-most in the NFL during that span. However, he could struggle against a tough 49ers defense that's given up just 16.4 fantasy points per game to opposing quarterbacks through five contests."}},"ownership":{"activityLevel":null,"auctionValueAverage":0.04,"auctionValueAverageChange":0.01,"averageDraftPosition":168.84,"averageDraftPositionPercentChange":0.04,"date":1792683043033,"leagueType":0,"percentChange":0.28,"percentOwned":12.78,"percentStarted":5.75},"proTeamId":1,"rankings":{"0":[{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":6,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":11,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":31,"rankSourceId":5,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":10,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":3,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":12,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":9,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":31,"rankSourceId":7,"rankType":"STANDARD","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":31,"rankSourceId":7,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0}],"2":[{"auctionValue":0,"published":false,"rank":32,"rankSourceId":6,"rankType":"PPR","slotId":0},{"auctionValue":0,"publishe