n a minimal portion of the Falcons' offensive game plan in the Week 4 matchup against the Saints, Through three weeks, Branch has caught three of four targets while playing 45 offensive snaps. Despite not having much competition in Atlanta's WR room, the rookie wideout likely won't have fantasy value without finding the end zone in Week 4. Additionally, Branch could struggle against a good New Orleans secondary that's allowed just 6.2 yards per pass attempt this season.","5":"Zachariah Branch's offensive role could continue to grow in the Falcons' Week 5 matchup against the Ravens. Branch has received two targets in each of his last three games, even out-targeting Olamide Zaccheaus over the last two weeks (four to three). Additionally, Branch played a career-high 23% of the Falcons' offensive snaps in the Week 4 win over the Saints, suggesting his offensive role may be growing. He's also in for a favorable Week 5 matchup against a Ravens secondary that's given up 734 receiving yards to wideouts through four contests this season, the sixth-most in the NFL.","6":"Zachariah Branch will likely play a complimentary role in Atlanta's receiving corps during the Week 6 matchup against the Bears. Branch has been more involved in the Falcons' offensive game plan over the last two weeks, catching all four of his targets for 25 yards. He appears to have overtaken Olamide Zaccheaus in the wide-receiver room but likely won't have much fantasy value without scoring a touchdown. That being said, Branch could succeed against a Bears defense that's giving up 10.4 yards per target to opposing WRs this season, the most in the NFL.","7":"Zachariah Branch's offensive role could continue to grow as the Falcons' face the 49ers in Week 7. Branch has caught all six of his targets over the last three weeks, accumulating 34 receiving yards. He appears to have emerged as Atlanta's No. 3 wideout, as Olamide Zaccheaus hasn't caught a pass since the Week 3 win over the Packers. Regardless, Branch 